/** @page mlreleasehistory ml Module Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    @section ml_3_0 ml Module Version 3.0
    - initial release
    - the files read and written for ONNX models are subject to the filesystem sandbox of the calling program: the
      model, its external data, the optimized model and the profile, and the files named by ONNX Runtime options;
      with a sandbox, content identity capture is always required, so that ONNX Runtime only reads bytes the sandbox
      allowed, and only ONNX Runtime options that name no file, or whose file is checked, may be set; see
      @ref ml_onnx_sandbox
    - the content identity of an ORT format model is complete: an ORT format model cannot have external data, so its
      content is its bytes, and a model whose content is captured is loaded in the format in which it was captured
    - the filesystem sandbox check of ONNX content identity capture honors a policy barrier established with
      \c SandboxManager::callWithSystemPolicy()
*/
